{
    "background_story": "Salma was a young artist with a passion for music and poetry. She had been pining for her childhood sweetheart, Alejandro, who had left their small town to pursue a career in the city. Despite the distance, Salma's love for him only grew stronger. She poured her heart out in her art, writing songs and poems that spoke of longing and yearning. Her music became a sensation in the local scene, with many interpreting her lyrics as a reflection of her own unrequited love. As the years went by, Salma's pining for Alejandro never faded, but it did inspire some of her most beautiful and haunting works. Though they had lost touch, Salma's art kept the memory of their love alive, a testament to the enduring power of true devotion.",
